{
  "answer_markdown": "Yes, Mistral supports a **moderations feature** for content classification and safety checks. Specifically:\n\n- Two dedicated models support **moderations**:\n  - Mistral Moderation (`mistral-moderation-2411`) [1].\n  - Mistral Moderation 2 (`mistral-moderation-2603`) [1].\n\n- These models can classify text into categories such as illegal activities, hateful/harassing content, or unqualified advice [14].\n\n- The **moderations** feature is accessible via the `/v1/moderations` endpoint for text moderation and `/v1/chat/moderations` for chat-based moderation [6, 7, 8].\n\n- Example API calls for moderations are provided in the documentation [15, 17].\n\n- Additionally, chat completions can use the `safe_prompt` flag for a basic level of moderation [11].\n\n- Batch processing also supports moderations via the `/v1/moderations` endpoint [9].",

  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Mistral Moderation (`mistral-moderation-2411`), Mistral Moderation 2 (`mistral-moderation-2603`)"
    },
