  "answer_markdown": "Mistral provides two models capable of converting text into numerical vector embeddings (the \"number lists\" used for semantic comparison in computers):\n\n1. **`mistral-embed`** – A general-purpose embedding model for text, generating 1024-dimensional vectors for semantic search, clustering, and classification tasks [2][4][5][6].\n\n   Example usage (Python):\n   ```python\n   embeddings_batch_response = client.embeddings.create(\n       model=\"mistral-embed\",\n       inputs=[\"Embed this sentence.\", \"As well as this one.\"]\n   )\n   ```\n\n2. **`codestral-embed`** – A specialized embedding model for code, designed to convert code snippets into vector representations for semantic code search, duplicate detection, and analytics [2][10].\n\n   Example usage (Python):\n   ```python\n   embeddings_batch_response = client.embeddings.create(\n       model=\"codestral-embed\",\n       inputs=[\"def hello():\", \"print('world')\"]\n   )\n   ```\n\nBoth models output vectors that can be compared using distance metrics (e.g., Euclidean distance, cosine similarity) to determine semantic similarity [5].",
