  "answer_markdown": "In **Mistral Vibe Code Web**, uncommitted GitHub sandbox files **cannot be resumed** once the session ends or becomes inactive. Here’s what happens and how to proceed:\n\n1. **Session lifecycle**: When a session ends (due to completion, timeout, or error), the sandbox is **deleted**, and all uncommitted files in it are lost [3][5][11]. Only GitHub branches, commits, and pull requests persist in your repository [3][12].\n\n2. **No resume capability**: Once the sandbox is deprovisioned, the session **cannot be resumed**—this applies to both web and CLI sessions [3][4][11].\n\n3. **Workaround**: To continue working on uncommitted changes, you must:\n   - Start a **new session** in Vibe Code Web [3][11].\n   - If using the CLI, resume the session with `vibe --continue` or `vibe --resume SESSION_ID` (requires logging enabled) [13].\n\n4. **Key limitation**: The sandbox is **ephemeral** and isolated to the session [5][9]. No local or session-specific files persist beyond its lifecycle.\n\n> **Note**: For local file persistence, use the **CLI or VS Code extension** instead of Vibe Code Web [3][15].",
